      "content": "wait, you say the dissent's arguments are \"legally flawed\" as if it's a fact. but shouldn't there be a formal legal basis for their view on substantive due process? i'm confused why you're framing it as if their logic is just wrong instead of just a different interpretation of the 14th amendment.",
